---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/href';
import { graph } from '../lib/graph';

const g = graph();
const reviewed = [...g.nodes.values()].filter((n) =>
  ['reviewed', 'co_authored'].includes(n.tribal_review?.status ?? ''),
).length;
const suggested = g.edges.filter((e) => e.status === 'proposed').length;
---

<Page
  title="About"
  lede="A free, public record of United States treaty law with Native nations, built to point attention and support toward Land Back."
>
  <h2>Who made this</h2>
  <p>
    Living Law, Living Land was created by Benjamin Life (@omniharmonic). It is not Indigenous-led.
    It does not speak for any nation, and it is not a substitute for what nations say about
    themselves. It is an attempt to make the public record easy to see and hard to ignore, and to
    hand that record back to the nations it concerns.
  </p>
  <h2>Where things stand</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Pages reviewed by a Native nation: <strong>{reviewed}</strong>. Every nation’s page can be{' '}
      <a href={href('/claim/')}>claimed</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Links suggested by matching names or dates and not yet reviewed by a person:{' '}
      <strong>{suggested.toLocaleString('en-US')}</strong>. Each is labeled.
    </li>
    <li>Legal review: not yet. Nothing here is legal advice.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>How sure we are</h2>
  <p>
    Every record carries a confidence level and its sources. Details that were not yet checked
    against a source are marked where they appear. Where sources disagree, we show the disagreement
    rather than choosing. See <a href={href('/methods/')}>methods</a>.
  </p>
  <h2>Open data</h2>
  <p>
    The code is MIT licensed and the project’s own text and data are CC BY 4.0, credited to Benjamin
    Life (@omniharmonic). The complete data, the build, and every change are public at
    <a href="https://github.com/omniharmonic/treaty-land-atlas">
      github.com/omniharmonic/treaty-land-atlas
    </a>
    . Text a nation contributes stays under the terms that nation sets.
  </p>
  <h2>Support</h2>
  <p>
    This site takes no money. To support land return, see{' '}
    <a href={href('/support/')}>how to help</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
